issue_context.body:
as titled, I'd like to have `path` in the fastify Request object
```js
fastify.get('/foo', function (req, reply) {
  reply.send({path: req.path}) // <--- this is '/foo'
})
```

comments:
I would say provide the path as it is configured for the handler. For example,

```js
const routes = function (instance, opts, next) {
  instance.get('/bar', (req, reply) => {
    reply.send(req.path) // '=> '/bar'
  })
}

fastify.register(routes, {prefix: '/foo'})
```
